{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147750-reason-for-a-kindred-to-engage-in-philanthropy","id":1147750,"title":"Reason for a Kindred to engage in philanthropy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-07T07:07:00-07:00","id":1147750,"title":"Reason for a Kindred to engage in philanthropy?","content":"Excuse me, but as I understand it, A kindred gains more fore maintaining his humanity by personally helping one highschool drop out study for a GED test. then donating a sum of money to help dozens get into college.<br /> <br /> I understand this is because of the personal human connection, but it brings to mind, is their a reason for a wealthy kindred to engage in philanthropy?<br /> <br /> best reason I can see is as a front for this or that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T07:32:57-07:00","id":1147756,"title":"","content":"Beyond cultivating an image among the mortal community? There are a few reasons.<br /> <br /> 1.) By establishing them self as a pillar of the community, it will make hunters think twice about attacking you, or the community might throw hunters off your track.<br /> <br /> 2.) My personal favorite, the kindred is actually engaging in philanthropy because they want to help people; not every kindred is going to be evil all the time. Sure, they'd be higher humanity, but not all kindred have low humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T07:54:22-07:00","id":1147764,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with number 2, but again what I said helping one highschool drop out prepare to get their GED will be more effective at maintaining your humanity, then donating money to help dozens of students with college.<br /> <br /> <br /> or you saying a high humanity kindred will naturally engage in philanthropy anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T07:56:05-07:00","id":1147766,"title":"","content":"In one setting, I had a vampire helping in famine relief, because he didn't like hunger and didn't think it should win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T09:40:23-07:00","id":1147796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147750-reason-for-a-kindred-to-engage-in-philanthropy#post1147750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me, but as I understand it, A kindred gains more fore maintaining his humanity by personally helping one highschool drop out study for a GED test. then donating a sum of money to help dozens get into college.<br /> <br /> I understand this is because of the personal human connection, but it brings to mind, is their a reason for a wealthy kindred to engage in philanthropy?<br /> <br /> best reason I can see is as a front for this or that</div> </div> </div> </div>The same reason drug cartels and king-pings build schools and hospitals: connections, influence and bribery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T09:41:50-07:00","id":1147797,"title":"","content":"Don't forget social engineering.<br /> \u200bFor example a Vampire helps improve the security of his haven by improving his neighborhood in ways that prevent crime, without drawing undue attention to that haven with obvious guards or bars on the window.<br /> Also Vampires need to feed and like any good farmer that means seeing to the health and well being of your animals.<br /> \u200bWhat kind of neighborhood does the Vampire want to live in? Is he content to walk trash littered streets? Does he enjoy being surrounded by people borne down by despair? Does he find derelict buildings, derelict people, gang bangers and street walkers visually appealing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:12:03-07:00","id":1147806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147750-reason-for-a-kindred-to-engage-in-philanthropy?p=1147797#post1147797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget social engineering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh ye neonates, the word you are looking for is 'politics.' :P<br /> <br /> On topic, given touchstones can be non-human and can take the form of locations or abstraction, I wager that it is possible to treat help on a grand scale as similar to the personal connection. However, I'd likely insist that the activity be 'made real' by pageantry and that it is limited to the types of people for whom beliefs are more real. A down-to-earth kindred might find indirect charity to less engaging that active help, despite being a very good person. The big answer to this question though would take us into the thorny world of psychology of the self, so my little answer is it works for the highly cerebral kindred but nobody else. Cerebral does not mean smart; just a 'theory first' kind of kindred. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:34:23-07:00","id":1147812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147750-reason-for-a-kindred-to-engage-in-philanthropy?p=1147764#post1147764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd agree with number 2, but again what I said helping one highschool drop out prepare to get their GED will be more effective at maintaining your humanity, then donating money to help dozens of students with college.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be more effective but it also takes much more time and forces them into a level of closeness they might not want to deal with. You help that kid, they become a target for your enemies. Even a random act of violence can end with your work undone and you frenzying wildly at perceived perpetrators. Maybe it even happens in front of you and there you are with the only thing that can keep them from truly dying, at the cost of your humanity.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, throw some money at a school and you can enjoy a closeness with the school, even have favorite students you might watch over secretly without actually getting too close. You get influence with the school, without being influenced by it in kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-07-2017, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:42:01-07:00","id":1147854,"title":"","content":"Humanity isn't morality. It also isn't really an IC concept; no vampire is going to do something because it &quot;maintains&quot; their &quot;Humanity&quot; stat.<br /> <br /> As to the question at hand: Why does anyone do philanthropy?<br /> <br /> Because they feel it's the right thing to do, so they look good, for tax breaks, etc. Vampires used to be people. They can have all the same motivations as people do. Just because there's no mechanical benefit doesn't mean there's no reason a vampire would want to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T15:36:13-07:00","id":1147874,"title":"","content":"&quot;Local philanthropist donates millions to AIDS prevention research&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Philanthropist donates a large sum to local hospital blood bank&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Millionaire help cure the homeless of disease&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeahhh... Philanthropy for philanthropy's sake isn't exactly their style","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T16:15:07-07:00","id":1147880,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> I was saying that the vampire with more of a connection to their humanity would probably be more likely to do the philanthropy bit to help the community. Of course, high humanity doesn't mean they'll be a philanthropist, and low humanity doesn't mean they wouldn't be a philanthropist. A low humanity vampire would probably focus on what they gain from it, but so could the high humanity vampire.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12561_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12561\" data-vbnamecard=\"12561\">Shawarbaaz</a> Not every kindred will commit philanthropy for philanthropy's sake. On that hand, most normal humans probably don't either. Vampires used to be normal humans, so some things about humanity can be taken in consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T17:01:52-07:00","id":1147888,"title":"","content":"Does dominating rich people in Wall Street into drawing thousands in cash from ATMs, which you then put in mailboxes of poor families in bad neighbourhoods count as philanthropy ? Because it sounds like the kind of things some ventrue neonate might do to inflate their ego and good conscience for virtually no effort. Like, &quot;Alright, so maybe I frenzied all over this hobo the other week and killed him, but it's okay because I did get Ms Jones and her three kids a box of caviar for Christmas... No, I did not know Ms Jones did not celebrate Christmas, but she'll just open it for New Year's eve then, and anyway what have YOU done for the community this month, besides apparently trying to reduce the rat population in the sewers ? Newsflash, they reproduce faster than you can eat them !&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T17:07:24-07:00","id":1147890,"title":"","content":"I want to play that Venture. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:19:29-07:00","id":1155401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147750-reason-for-a-kindred-to-engage-in-philanthropy?p=1147854#post1147854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity isn't morality. It also isn't really an IC concept; no vampire is going to do something because it &quot;maintains&quot; their &quot;Humanity&quot; stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>While no vamp would put it in the terms you used, I'd argue maintaining humanity is a conscious effort on their part, and thus an IC consideration for those who do so. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the question at hand: Why does anyone do philanthropy?<br /> <br /> Because they feel it's the right thing to do, so they look good, for tax breaks, etc. Vampires used to be people. They can have all the same motivations as people do. Just because there's no mechanical benefit doesn't mean there's no reason a vampire would want to do it. </div> </div> </div>This part, I fully agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:25:17-07:00","id":1155836,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's also the time commitment factor.<br /> <br /> Philanthropy tends to actually be pretty time efficient. It gives you more time to do your thing, rather than spending an hour or two every night tutoring some schmuck.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}